WEBVTT

00:00:01.590 --> 00:00:05.230
Satoshi, who aims to battle
the Supreme Monarch, Dande...

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.240
And Go, who dreams of catching every Pokémon
to work his way up to Mew...

00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:15.530
This is the story of
their lives and adventures.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.750
This is the Sakuragi Institute.

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:27.000
Late at night,
while everyone is fast asleep...

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.600
...a certain Pokémon
is up and about.

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:09.910
Shishi, shishishi!

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:27.550
Let’s start with just one, shi...

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:13.030
Breakfast... really is the best!

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:15.310
What about lunch and dinner, then?

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.350
Well, lunch is super-tasty...

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.690
...and dinner is hyper-tasty!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.030
What’s that supposed to mean?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.380
Ah... What a nice scent.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:29.790
Good weather, and good moods.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:34.420
Looks like we’re in for
a quiet, peaceful day.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:38.670
Bad news, Director Sakuragi!

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:39.170
Ow, ow!
Bad news, Director Sakuragi!

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:41.460
What’re we gonna do...?!

00:04:41.460 --> 00:04:43.420
What’s wrong, you two?

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:45.860
What’s wrong... you say?

00:04:45.860 --> 00:04:52.560
The data... The Pokémon data
you put so much effort into collecting is gone!

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:54.310
What?!

00:04:58.320 --> 00:04:59.910
It’s true.

00:04:59.910 --> 00:05:02.320
And it’s only data on Isshu
that’s missing.

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:04.330
Can we recover it?

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:07.320
I’ll try,
but it could be pretty hard.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:08.830
No way...

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.610
That can’t be right!

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:13.400
Did... Did it fall out anywhere?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.580
Hey, data! Hey! Data!

00:05:23.940 --> 00:05:25.100
C’mon, data!

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:25.810
Wait...

00:05:26.170 --> 00:05:27.760
Data doesn't just “fall out”!

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:28.760
Huh?

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.650
I wonder where our data went...

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:48.280
The Director said there were traces of
someone accessing the Institute’s main data.

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:52.090
Maybe someone
went and deleted it.

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:55.220
Here.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.060
For Jimeleon.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.480
Thanks.

00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:00.960
How’s Jimeleon been?

00:06:00.960 --> 00:06:05.840
He’s been eating plenty every day.
He’s cooped up, but doing fine!

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.600
You’re covered in mud!

00:06:32.690 --> 00:06:35.120
This one spot is muddy...?

00:06:45.360 --> 00:06:48.100
There. It’s all done.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:51.410
We even changed
all of our passwords.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:55.390
With all the extra security,
we can rest easy now!

00:07:03.320 --> 00:07:05.610
Did I imagine that?

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:18.650
Wild!
I got all of their new passwords, shi!

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:20.900
Shishishishi!

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:45.000
A-n-d... delete, shi!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:07.820
Hey...
You don’t have to sulk so much...

00:09:07.820 --> 00:09:11.360
How could we <i>not</i> be
sulking right now?

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:14.370
We spent the whole day
improving security yesterday...

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:19.020
But it was breached like
it was nothing, and now...

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:22.290
The Galar data was deleted!

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:24.080
No...

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:41.370
You worked so hard
collecting so much valuable data...

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:42.580
I’m so sorry...

00:09:43.170 --> 00:09:45.640
Director Sakuragi,
you shouldn’t be apologizing!

00:09:46.170 --> 00:09:49.110
Whoever deleted it is to blame!

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:53.190
He’s right! Director!
We didn’t go far enough!

00:09:53.190 --> 00:09:57.200
Let’s do it!
Impenetrable super-security!

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:59.660
Okay... Let’s go!

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:03.860
Go for it!

00:10:07.670 --> 00:10:10.550
You ate plenty again today,
huh, Jimeleon?

00:10:16.020 --> 00:10:20.050
Hey, um... We’ve been dealing with a problem
at the Institute the past few days...

00:10:20.740 --> 00:10:24.310
Someone’s been deleting the data
we collected together.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:27.310
Even our data from Galar.

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:30.860
That data...

00:10:31.290 --> 00:10:33.850
It was our memories
with Pokémon.

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:36.360
Jimeleon...

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:40.470
Lots of the memories I made with you
were in there, too.

00:10:40.990 --> 00:10:42.690
I...

00:10:42.690 --> 00:10:45.080
I can’t let them get away with this.

00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:12.270
Pocket Monsters!

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:42.890
Nobody around, huh...?

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:53.350
No way...

00:12:03.720 --> 00:12:05.740
Jimeleon?! What are y—

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:26.550
Something’s there!

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.130
A Kakuleon?!

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:40.230
Kakuleon! Color Swap Pokémon!
Normal type!

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:42.940
It can freely change its body’s color!

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:45.700
The zigzag pattern on its belly
doesn’t change!

00:12:46.060 --> 00:12:49.130
Wait... It was this Kakuleon
who deleted our data?!

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:50.700
That’s right, shi.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:52.260
It can speak?!

00:12:52.260 --> 00:12:54.830
We deleted your data, shi!

00:12:54.830 --> 00:12:57.990
You should’ve noticed sooner, shi.

00:12:57.990 --> 00:13:00.460
Shi, shishishi, shi!

00:13:06.140 --> 00:13:08.670
Yabashi counters, shi!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.190
Are you okay, Jimeleon?!

00:13:15.190 --> 00:13:16.900
See ya, shi!

00:13:16.900 --> 00:13:18.640
Man...

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:21.530
Yeah, got it!

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:30.780
What is it...?

00:13:34.710 --> 00:13:35.500
Huh?

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:38.920
Stop, Kakuleon!

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:39.500
Go!

00:13:41.000 --> 00:13:42.910
That thing’s been
deleting the data!

00:13:42.910 --> 00:13:44.470
What?!

00:13:54.430 --> 00:13:55.510
Stop!

00:14:01.730 --> 00:14:03.370
Don’t let it get away,
Jimeleon!

00:14:03.370 --> 00:14:05.110
Wild!

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:08.610
You don’t know
when to give up, shi!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:10.050
What?

00:14:10.950 --> 00:14:12.810
I’m Yabashi!

00:14:12.810 --> 00:14:17.580
The man who’s gonna make a wild Institute
way better than Sakuragi Institute, shi!

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:20.170
Better than Sakuragi Institute?!

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:25.460
So... You deleted our data
because it was in your way?!

00:14:25.460 --> 00:14:27.470
Exactly, shi.

00:14:27.470 --> 00:14:30.210
Well then...
Sneak Attack, shi!

00:14:31.450 --> 00:14:32.550
Jimeleon!

00:14:32.550 --> 00:14:36.930
Wild! Your Jimeleon’s
so weak it’s wild, shi!

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:40.900
In comparison, my Kakuleon’s
had a special training regimen, shi,

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:45.440
and it’s much stronger and smarter
than the average one, shi!

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:49.070
Now then, Kakuleon! Bind!

00:14:49.070 --> 00:14:50.700
Pound, Jimeleon!

00:14:57.450 --> 00:14:59.040
Don’t give up, Jimeleon!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:01.040
Shi, shishishi!

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:14.180
Jimeleon!

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:18.430
Are you okay, Jimeleon?!

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:23.440
Shi, shishishi!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:28.360
All beat up and in a wild spot,
so let’s give it a good wallop, shi!

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:34.070
Look out! Run for it, Go!

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:39.410
Don’t worry! I’ll protect you!

00:15:40.110 --> 00:15:43.250
Wanna come with me?

00:15:43.250 --> 00:15:49.720
People may call you timid,
but I think it’s good to protect yourself!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:53.110
I’ll be with you in spirit,
even when we’re apart!

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:05.610
Ahh... This is wild!

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:29.170
You evolved...? Jimeleo—

00:16:30.440 --> 00:16:34.260
Inteleon’s data will be
added to the Index!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.950
Inteleon!

00:16:49.190 --> 00:16:52.030
Wild! Kakuleon,
use Iron Tail!

00:17:08.000 --> 00:17:10.190
Wh-Whoa...

00:17:10.190 --> 00:17:13.060
You’re super cool, Inteleon!

00:17:16.950 --> 00:17:20.510
This is wild,
the ultimate in wild!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:22.270
Now you’ve gone and made me...

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:24.770
...run for it, shi!

00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:32.840
Snipe Shot!

00:17:36.660 --> 00:17:39.490
Wh-Wh-Wha...?!

00:17:39.490 --> 00:17:43.460
Wild! This is wild!

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:45.750
Shi?

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:48.570
All right!

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:07.060
What’s with that wild face?!

00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.940
Stop that, you smug Inteleon!

00:18:09.940 --> 00:18:12.830
My Kakuleon is a pure lady!

00:18:12.830 --> 00:18:14.320
Don’t you dare try anything, shi!

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:19.160
Inteleon!

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:22.080
Hey, Yabashi!

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.670
How could you delete our data?

00:18:25.770 --> 00:18:26.780
Don’t blame me, shi!

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:28.960
Blame your
shoddy security, shi!

00:18:28.960 --> 00:18:31.010
What did you say...?!

00:18:31.010 --> 00:18:32.950
Go, you say something, too!

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:36.410
I guess it’s too late
now that it’s already gone...

00:18:38.160 --> 00:18:42.150
But that data
was really important to us.

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.350
I want you to realize that.

00:18:48.580 --> 00:18:54.080
Was I correct in hearing that
you deleted our data?

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:02.990
Th-The one and only...
Mister Professor Sakuragi, sir!

00:19:06.750 --> 00:19:09.930
This is wild,
the ultimate in wild, <i>again,</i> shi!

00:19:09.930 --> 00:19:13.630
I never imagined I’d be standing before
the one and only Mister Professor Sakuragi Sir!

00:19:13.630 --> 00:19:16.320
“The one and only
Mister Professor Sir”...

00:19:16.320 --> 00:19:17.510
What’s going on?

00:19:17.950 --> 00:19:20.380
I’m a huge fan!
Please sign this!

00:19:20.960 --> 00:19:22.340
A huge fan?!

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.010
And you are?

00:19:24.010 --> 00:19:27.400
Yabayabashi.
But call me Yabashi!

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:30.600
Yabashi.
Let’s be honest here.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.600
It isn’t really gone, is it?

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:34.730
Our data.

00:19:37.380 --> 00:19:41.070
Y-Yes. It’s still there.

00:19:42.540 --> 00:19:43.530
I thought so.

00:19:43.970 --> 00:19:50.390
I... I really like and admire
your Institute.

00:19:50.910 --> 00:19:56.500
I just wanted the one and only
Mister Professor Sakuragi Sir to notice me.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:19:58.960
And that’s why you deleted our data.

00:19:58.960 --> 00:20:02.310
I-I’m sorry, shi!

00:20:02.890 --> 00:20:05.050
So that was it.

00:20:13.810 --> 00:20:15.460
Will this do?

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.830
Well, problem solved!

00:20:38.440 --> 00:20:40.710
The data’s back!

00:20:51.280 --> 00:20:54.350
What a relief... Really.

00:21:09.130 --> 00:21:10.740
Inteleon?

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:27.220
I’m not gonna cry!

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:32.170
Bidding tears farewell,

00:21:32.170 --> 00:21:36.890
Go and Inteleon look ready to start
a new kind of relationship.

00:21:36.890 --> 00:21:40.790
I can’t wait to see what
tomorrow brings.

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.570
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:23:09.570 --> 00:23:10.870
Go!

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:12.810
Eclipse Castle?

00:23:12.810 --> 00:23:17.080
They’ve cherished Eefee and Blacky
as special creatures for eons.

00:23:17.080 --> 00:23:18.550
Eefee and Blacky?

00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:20.700
They’re both evolutions of Eevee.

00:23:20.700 --> 00:23:21.870
I want to go!

00:23:21.870 --> 00:23:23.220
Right, Eevee?

00:23:24.310 --> 00:23:25.380
I’ll go, too!

00:23:25.380 --> 00:23:27.420
Go and have fun,
all of you together.

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:28.750
All right!

00:23:28.750 --> 00:23:30.300
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:33.760
The Moon and Sun,
Koharu and Haruhi
